# CODEOWNERS — LQ.AI
# ============================================================
# Path-based reviewer assignments. The most recent matching
# pattern takes precedence; later patterns override earlier ones.
#
# EVERY TEAM NAMED IN THIS FILE MUST EXIST IN THE ORG.
# GitHub silently ignores an entry that names a team which does
# not exist: the routing does not happen and no error is raised.
# This file previously named four teams (maintainers, security,
# counsel, practicing-attorneys), none of which existed, so no
# review was routed anywhere. See ADR 0034.
#
# Specialist routing returns here as each team is created AND
# staffed — not before. The intent is recorded in comments below
# so it is not lost; a comment is honest, a phantom team is not.
#
# CODEOWNERS only holds a PR if the branch ruleset requires
# code-owner review. See ADR 0034 decision 5.
#
# References:
# - PR review process: ../CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-request-process
# - Review timelines:  ../CONTRIBUTING.md#review-timelines
# - Skill review process: ../skills/CONTRIBUTING.md
# - ADR 0034: ../docs/adr/0034-review-capacity-and-reviewer-roles.md
# ============================================================

# Default — all changes require maintainer review
*                              @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers

# ---------- Repository-level governance ----------
/LICENSE                       @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md            @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/GOVERNANCE.md                 @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md               @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/SECURITY.md                   @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS            @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers

# ---------- Security-sensitive paths ----------
# The Inference Gateway holds the security boundary. Until a
# security team exists, these paths are held for maintainer
# review with the security-path checklist applied — which is
# weaker than a dedicated security reviewer, and is stated that
# way in CLAUDE.md rather than overclaimed.
# TODO(ADR 0034): add @LegalQuants/lq-ai-security when staffed.
/gateway/                      @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/docs/security/                @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/.github/workflows/            @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers

# ---------- Compliance documentation ----------
# Compliance Alignment Pack mappings affect procurement posture.
# TODO(ADR 0034): add a counsel team when one exists.
/docs/compliance/              @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/docs/procurement/             @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers

# ---------- Skills (legal substance) ----------
# Skills containing legal substance require practicing-attorney
# review in addition to maintainer review. That requirement is
# enforced by the process in skills/CONTRIBUTING.md and the
# attorney-reviewer pool, NOT by this file, until a
# practicing-attorneys team exists.
# TODO(ADR 0034): add @LegalQuants/lq-ai-attorneys when staffed.
/skills/                       @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/skills/CONTRIBUTING.md        @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers

# ---------- Canonical specification ----------
# PRD changes affect every downstream artifact.
/docs/PRD.md                   @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/docs/architecture.md          @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/docs/adr/                     @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
/docs/skill-authoring-guide.md @LegalQuants/lq-ai-maintainers
